{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"22 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,10.666,3.651,3.268,"Marico"],[13.889,14.731,37.149,2.373,2.124,"A copra windfall priced as compounding"],[13.889,20.845,52.964,1.809,1.634,"Marico rose 10% the day after its Q2 FY27 results and is 15% above the pre-"],[13.889,22.289,52.959,1.809,1.634,"results close (NIFTY +10%). At ₹917 it trades on 54x FY27E and 49x FY28E"],[13.889,23.733,52.934,1.809,1.634,"EPS, above its own three-year average of 47x forward earnings. The quarter was"],[13.889,25.177,52.954,1.809,1.634,"strong: revenue rose 13% to ₹3,897 cr on 10% India volume growth and 13%"],[13.889,26.621,52.931,1.809,1.634,"constant-currency growth abroad, EBITDA rose 27% to ₹709 cr, and"],[13.889,28.065,52.931,1.809,1.634,"management raised FY27 EBITDA growth guidance to the mid-twenties. We"],[13.889,29.509,52.339,1.809,1.634,"rate the shares Underweight with a Dec-27 target of ₹750, 18% below the price."],[13.889,31.995,52.954,1.809,1.634,"Two things flatter the 31% profit growth. Gross margin rose 600bp to 48.1%"],[13.889,33.439,52.931,1.809,1.634,"because copra is 35% below last year’s peak: Parachute sold 13% more volume"],[13.889,34.883,52.936,1.809,1.634,"for about 1% more revenue after price cuts. That is a commodity cycle, not"],[13.889,36.328,52.964,1.809,1.634,"pricing power. And the tax rate fell to 17.2% from 21.5% on a ₹95 cr deferred-"],[13.889,37.772,52.931,1.809,1.634,"tax credit (₹157 cr in H1); at last year’s rate profit would have grown 24%. A&P"],[13.889,39.216,52.931,1.809,1.634,"rose 44% to 11.6% of revenue. We take FY27 EBITDA at guidance (+25%, H2"],[13.889,40.684,52.936,1.809,1.634,"margin 18.3% vs 16.4%), tax at FY26’s 20.4%: FY27E EPS ₹16.89 against"],[13.889,42.128,52.934,1.809,1.634,"consensus ₹17.16. For FY28E we model EBITDA +13%, below management’s"],[13.889,43.572,28.135,1.809,1.634,"mid-teens, and EPS ₹18.70 against ₹19.74."],[13.889,46.034,52.931,1.809,1.634,"The target averages 47x, Marico’s own three-year average, on EPS for the"],[13.889,47.502,52.931,1.809,1.634,"twelve months after Dec-27 (₹20.5), or ₹964, and a ten-year FCFE DCF at an"],[13.889,48.946,52.936,1.809,1.634,"11% cost of equity and 6.5% terminal growth plus net cash, or ₹527 (₹670 at"],[13.889,50.39,52.931,1.809,1.634,"10%). The legs are far apart. The multiple leg alone is +5%; the DCF needs free"],[13.889,51.834,52.931,1.809,1.634,"cash flow to grow 19.6% a year to FY37 against our 9.9%. Consensus of ₹965"],[13.889,53.278,52.964,1.809,1.634,"(38 analysts, 37 buy) is 5% above the price. What would prove us wrong: mid-"],[13.889,54.722,52.931,1.809,1.634,"teens EBITDA growth in FY28 with copra staying low, which would hold"],[13.889,56.167,52.931,1.809,1.634,"today’s 49x FY28E. The main risk to the business is the reverse: a copra"],[13.889,57.611,30.372,1.809,1.634,"rebound with A&P already at 12% of revenue."],[13.889,60.098,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[15.268,68.709,1.489,1.022,0.915,"600"],[15.268,66.942,1.489,1.022,0.915,"700"],[15.268,65.174,1.489,1.022,0.915,"800"],[15.268,63.407,1.489,1.022,0.915,"900"],[14.451,61.639,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,000"],[17.913,69.404,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.539,69.404,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.326,69.404,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.08,69.404,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[18.622,70.575,3.275,1.275,1.111,"Marico ("],[21.9,70.601,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[22.513,70.575,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[25.597,70.575,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.53,71.735,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[26.036,71.735,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[30.042,71.735,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,71.735,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,72.8,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[19.611,72.8,2.811,1.387,1.209,"22.7%"],[24.565,72.8,2.811,1.387,1.209,"17.9%"],[29.123,72.8,2.26,1.387,1.209,"6.8%"],[